|~ `::fail`, the step `!|` runs on an error alone, and what is declared
   under it: its constructor and its refusals.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:fail
  |~~ The fail track, `a !| b`: the step `b` runs on a failure alone,
      caught to its error at rest, and any other value passes it by, so
      it is where a failure is read, recovered or raised again, while
      `|` passes a failure by. `"x" | add 1 !| 0` answers `0`.

      In a quote the step is a record that wraps the quote of its one
      step, `~(!| get /kind) | first` answering `::fail~(get /kind)`.
      ::link~(::error | doc) ::link~(::qlang/errors | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps |~~ The quote of a step, built into the step `!| step`. ~~|
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ The payload of `::fail` is the quote of the step it wraps, so
            `~(get /kind) | tag ::fail` is the step `!| get /kind`.
            ::link~(::fail | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :ReadBackDiffersError
        |~~ The `::fail` prints as text that reads back as another step,
            or as none, and `:printed` is that text: it wraps one step, so
            a pipeline prints as `!| a | b`, where `!|` takes the first
            step alone, and an empty quote as no step. A pipeline under
            `!|` is written as a group,
            `~((get /kind | print)) | tag ::fail` the step
            `!| (get /kind | print)`.
            ::link~(::fail | doc)
        ~~|
    | proves :holdsItsStep
        |~~ The fail track holds its step as a quote. ~~|
        ~(~(!| get /kind) | first | payload | eq ~(get /kind))
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(42 | tag ::fail !| get [~(type) /actualType] | eq [::fail/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::number])
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/buildsTheStepOfAStep
        |~~ The quote of a step builds the step the fail track runs. ~~|
        ~(~(get /kind) | tag ::fail | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote | eq ~(!| get /kind))
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAPipelineOutsideAGroup
        |~~ A pipeline wrapped without a group prints as text that reads
            back as two steps.
        ~~|
        ~(~(a | b) | tag ::fail !| get [~(type) /printed] | eq [::fail/ReadBackDiffersError "!| a | b"])
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAnEmptyQuote
        |~~ An empty quote prints as text that reads back as no step. ~~|
        ~(~() | tag ::fail !| get [~(type) /printed] | eq [::fail/ReadBackDiffersError "!| "])
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/wrapsAPipelineInAGroup
        |~~ A pipeline in a group is the one step the fail track runs. ~~|
        ~(~((get /kind | print)) | tag ::fail | get [~(it)] | tag ::quote | eq ~(!| (get /kind | print)))
    | impl ::builtin{}

